{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4681","published":"2026-11-04T13:54:26Z","modified":"2026-11-04T14:00:03.051211037Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-119124"],"summary":"ImageMagick security update","details":"Use ImageMagick to create, edit, compose, or convert bitmap images. It can read and write images in a variety of formats (over 200) including PNG, JPEG, GIF, HEIC, TIFF, DPX, EXR, WebP, Postscript, PDF, and SVG. Use ImageMagick to resize, flip, mirror, rotate, distort, shear and transform images, adjust image colors, apply various special effects, or draw text, lines, polygons, ellipses and Bézier curves.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nImageMagick before 7.1.2-34 contains a heap-based buffer overflow in its -morph processing, where crafted images cause writes beyond the bounds of a heap buffer. An attacker can supply a crafted image that, when processed by a user with the -morph option, corrupts heap memory and crashes the application.(CVE-2026-119124)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/ImageMagick&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["ImageMagick-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-c++-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-c++-devel-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-debuginfo-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-debugsource-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-devel-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","ImageMagick-perl-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["ImageMagick-help-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.noarch.rpm"],"src":["ImageMagick-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["ImageMagick-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","ImageMagick-c++-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","ImageMagick-c++-devel-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","ImageMagick-debuginfo-7.1.2.35-1.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","ImageMagick-debugsource-7.1.2.35-1.oe24